Root cause: Pikaday's global keydown listener intercepts ArrowLeft regardless of focus, preventing default and adjusting date instead of caret movement.

Repair strategy: Add a condition to _onKeyChange to only process arrow keys when the associated input field has focus (or when the picker's field is the active element).

Expected accessibility effect: ArrowLeft will now move caret in other text fields, allowing users to correct text; keyboard navigation of date picker still works when the date field is focused.

Functional risks: Possibly breaking keyboard navigation for date picker when focus is within the picker but not on the input field (e.g., after clicking inside the calendar). However the date picker is bound to a separate container and the input may lose focus; users may need to click the input again to regain keyboard control. This is a minor regression mitigated by the fact that the date picker is usually used via the input field.

Verification requirements: Ensure that ArrowLeft in notes field moves caret and inserts space; ensure that ArrowLeft in delivery-date field still changes date; ensure that Enter/Esc still close picker; ensure that date picker still opens/closes correctly.

